<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qingzhou</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Qingzhou is a city in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shandong">Shandong</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, named after one of the ancient Nine Provinces and an important regional capital from the Han to the Ming. The nearby fortress of Guanggu was the capital of the Southern Yan state from about 400. In 1996 a hoard of some 400 Buddhist sculptures, many from the Northern Wei to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-qi">Northern Qi</a> periods, was found at the site of its Longxing Temple.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/qingzhou.jpg" alt="Qingzhou" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ngguls · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:20211114_%E9%9D%92%E5%B7%9E%E4%B8%89%E5%AE%98%E5%BA%99.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
